---
export const prerender = true;
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';

const title = 'Editorial Policy | JobVacancy.co.ke';
const description = 'How JobVacancy.co.ke sources, reviews and publishes job listings.';
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} path="/editorial-policy/" noindex>
  <Breadcrumbs items={[{ name: 'Home', href: '/' }, { name: 'Editorial Policy' }]} />
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-10 sm:px-6">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold text-brand-dark">Editorial Policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-400">Last updated: {new Date().toLocaleDateString('en-KE', { day: 'numeric', month: 'long', year: 'numeric' })}</p>
    <div class="prose prose-slate mt-6 max-w-none space-y-4 text-slate-700">
      <p>
        This policy explains where our job listings come from and how they're reviewed, so job seekers and employers
        know what to expect from JobVacancy.co.ke.
      </p>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-brand-dark">Where listings come from</h2>
      <p>
        Listings reach our site in two ways: (1) employers and recruiters submit a vacancy directly through our free
        <a href="/post-a-job/" class="font-semibold text-brand-orange">Post a Job</a> form, and (2) our team collects
        publicly posted vacancies from trusted recruitment sources — including NGO, government, teaching/TSC,
        remote/online, and international categories like cruise ship and teaching-abroad roles — to make sure job
        seekers see a fuller picture of what's available.
      </p>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-brand-dark">Human review before publication</h2>
      <p>
        Every listing — whether submitted directly or collected from another source — is reviewed by our team before
        it appears on the site. We check that a listing is for a genuine, currently open position, and reject or
        remove anything that is misleading, discriminatory, or that requests payment from applicants. See our
        <a href="/terms/" class="font-semibold text-brand-orange">Terms of Use</a> for the full posting rules.
      </p>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-brand-dark">AI-assisted summaries</h2>
      <p>
        Some listings include a short skills summary, an estimated salary range, or contextual career notes (for
        example, what to expect from a role in a given sector or location). These sections are generated with the
        help of automated tools at the time a listing is published, to help job seekers scan roles faster. They are
        a supplementary guide, not verified by the employer and not part of the original job description — the
        official role details always come from the employer's own listing text. See our
        <a href="/disclaimer/" class="font-semibold text-brand-orange">Disclaimer</a> for more on how to treat these
        estimates.
      </p>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-brand-dark">Corrections and removals</h2>
      <p>
        If you spot an outdated, inaccurate, or suspicious listing, email
        <a href="mailto:hr@jobvacancy.co.ke" class="font-semibold text-brand-orange">hr@jobvacancy.co.ke</a> with the
        job title and company name. We investigate every report and correct or remove listings that don't meet our
        standards. Roles are also archived automatically once they've been open for an extended period, to keep
        search results current.
      </p>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-brand-dark">Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions about this policy? Email <a href="mailto:hr@jobvacancy.co.ke" class="font-semibold text-brand-orange">hr@jobvacancy.co.ke</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
